  # ==========================================
  # SMOKE / POSITIVE SCENARIOS
  # ==========================================

  @Smoke @P0 @Auth @Positive @Login
  Scenario: Successful login with valid credentials
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    When the user enters valid email "testuser@example.com"
    And the user enters valid password "SecurePass123!"
    And the user clicks the "Login" button
    Then the user should be redirected to the dashboard
    And the navigation header should display the user's name
    And no error messages should be visible

  @Smoke @P0 @Auth @Positive @Logout
  Scenario: Successful logout from authenticated session
    Given the user is logged in with valid credentials
    When the user clicks the user menu
    And the user clicks "Logout"
    Then the user should be redirected to the login page
    And the session should be cleared
    And navigating to the dashboard should redirect to login

  @Smoke @P0 @Auth @Positive @PageLoad
  Scenario: Login page displays all required elements on load
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    Then the email input field should be visible
    And the password input field should be visible
    And the "Login" button should be visible and enabled
    And the application logo should be displayed
    And the page should use HTTPS protocol

  # ==========================================
  # NEGATIVE SCENARIOS
  # ==========================================

  @Negative @P0 @Auth @InvalidCredentials
  Scenario Outline: Login fails with invalid credentials
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    When the user enters email "<email>"
    And the user enters password "<password>"
    And the user clicks the "Login" button
    Then an error message should be displayed
    And the error message should not reveal which field is wrong
    And the user should remain on the login page

    Examples:
      | email                    | password       |
      | testuser@example.com     | WrongPass123!  |
      | unknown@example.com      | SecurePass123! |
      | invalid@example.com      | wrongpassword  |

  @Negative @P0 @Auth @Validation @EmptyFields
  Scenario: Login fails when email field is empty
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    When the user leaves the email field empty
    And the user enters "SecurePass123!" in the password field
    And the user clicks the "Login" button
    Then a validation error should appear on the email field
    And the error message should say "Email is required"
    And no API request should be made

  @Negative @P0 @Auth @Validation @EmptyFields
  Scenario: Login fails when password field is empty
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    When the user enters "testuser@example.com" in the email field
    And the user leaves the password field empty
    And the user clicks the "Login" button
    Then a validation error should appear on the password field
    And the error message should say "Password is required"
    And no API request should be made

  @Negative @P1 @Auth @Validation @InvalidFormat
  Scenario Outline: Login fails with invalid email format
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    When the user enters "<invalid_email>" in the email field
    And the user enters "SecurePass123!" in the password field
    And the user clicks the "Login" button
    Then a validation error should appear: "Please enter a valid email address"
    And the form should not be submitted

    Examples:
      | invalid_email          |
      | plaintext              |
      | missing@domain         |
      | @nodomain.com          |
      | spaces in@email.com    |
      | double@@domain.com     |
      | email@                 |

  @Negative @P0 @Auth @Security @AccountLock
  Scenario: Account gets locked after 5 consecutive failed login attempts
    Given the user navigates to the login page
    When the user attempts to login with wrong password 5 consecutive times
    Then the account should be temporarily locked
    And the error message should indicate the account is locked
    And even correct credentials should fail during lockout period
    And an unlock notification email should be sent to the registered email

  @Negative @P1 @Auth @Session @Timeout
  Scenario: Session expires after configured inactivity period
    Given the user is logged in with valid credentials
    When the user is inactive for the configured session timeout period
    And the user attempts any authenticated action
    Then the user should be redirected to the login page
    And the message "Your session has expired. Please log in again." should appear

